  "title": "Optimal Skill Selection for LLM Agents with Provable Bicriteria Guarantees",
  "summary": "This paper presents a method to select skill sets in LLM agents, ensuring that the selected skills maximize a monotone submodular benefit while accounting for context penalties, leading to improved performance and token efficiency. The proposed framework (Best Prefix Selection, BPS) provides a bicriteria $(1-1/e, 1)$ approximation with proven performance guarantees.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "The paper introduces Best Prefix Selection (BPS), a polynomial-time algorithm for skill selection in LLM agents.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "BPS achieves a bicriteria $(1-1/e, 1)$ approximation with optimal benefit coefficients.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "On the contamination-controlled BigCodeBench variant, BPS outperforms all baselines in terms of task success and token efficiency.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
